# The @qits scope lives in the platform's own npm repository, not on npmjs. Two lines, and two
# services: everything through qits-mirror's npmjs pull-through cache, ours from qits-artifacts'
# hosted registry. Both are the platform's public hosts, derived the same way everywhere (qits-731);
# the image build derives the identical pair from its own QITS_DOMAIN build-arg, and the lockfile is
# installed exactly as committed — there is no origin left to rewrite.
#
# Both hosts answer 401 without a credential. Put it in ~/.npmrc, keyed by the scheme-less URL:
#   //mirror.qits.wohlben.eu/npm/npmjs/:_authToken=...
#   //registry.qits.wohlben.eu/artifacts/npm/npm/:_authToken=...
#
# THIS FILE IS .dockerignore'd, DELIBERATELY. npm ranks a project .npmrc ABOVE ~/.npmrc, and the
# image build writes ~/.npmrc from the two registries it derives — so a copy of this file inside the
# build context would silently win and leave the install with no credential. See docker/Dockerfile
# and app.yml's Dockerfile contract.
registry=https://mirror.qits.wohlben.eu/npm/npmjs/
@qits:registry=https://registry.qits.wohlben.eu/artifacts/npm/npm/
